Link to their career hopes, maybe.

806
00:42:55,080 --> 00:42:59,310
And importantly, if they push back or disagree, really listen.

807
00:42:59,510 --> 00:43:00,170
Don't interrupt.

808
00:43:00,510 --> 00:43:01,210
Ask questions.

809
00:43:01,910 --> 00:43:04,750
Be open to adjusting your view if they make valid points.

810
00:43:04,810 --> 00:43:12,420
And you know, if we connect this to the bigger picture, even conflict, like direct team conflict, can actually be a chance for growth if it's handled with smart communication.

811
00:43:12,670 --> 00:43:18,790
That's a good way to look at it because, yeah, sometimes tensions flare up between team members, affects the work, the mood.

812
00:43:19,250 --> 00:43:20,240
How do you step into that?

813
00:43:20,380 --> 00:43:23,630
Well, the material often suggests starting with individual chats.

814
00:43:23,870 --> 00:43:25,430
Talk to each person separately first.

815
00:43:25,850 --> 00:43:28,750
Get their perspective without making them feel defensive in front of others.

816
00:43:29,430 --> 00:43:35,480
